From e334c17ba9bfbdbbbe5f7a989e2644b89edd2d97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noah Cylich <noahcylich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:17:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] temporal-MoE CUDA: trained routing on the device, streamed
 slots follow the router's window

k_route is the CUDA twin of ggml_temporal_route: per-layer window state on the device, router
logits in, window ids out, same rule and tie-breaking (cold fill top-K, then admit the best
non-resident iff its logit beats the worst resident, newcomer in slot K-1). The CUDA backend
accepts the ffn_moe_route custom op, so the decode graph stays one captured CUDA graph.

Under trained routing k_residency keeps its one-swap fast path and falls back to the
multi-swap scan when more than one selected expert is missing (first token of a sequence,
first decode token after a prefill). The expert-major prefill no longer re-masks the ids,
since they already are each token's window. llama_context resets the device window at
position 0. Counters and LLAMA_TEMPORAL_ROUTE_DUMP are read back from the device.
